<section class="setup">
    <h2>🛠️ Lab Setup: VLAN Configuration Mastery</h2>
    <p class="intro-text">
        Let's dive into Virtual LANs! This lab will teach you how to segment networks using VLANs for better security and performance.
    </p>

    <div class="setup-step">
        <div class="step-header">
            <span class="step-number">1</span>
            <h3>Build Your VLAN Foundation</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="step-content">
            <div class="instruction-card">
                <div class="instruction-icon">💻</div>
                <div class="instruction-text">
                    Create a new GNS3 project named: <span class="highlight">BLab2</span>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="visual-guide">
                <p><strong>Add these devices:</strong></p>
                <div class="device-grid">
                    <div class="device-item">
                        <div class="device-icon">🖥️</div>
                        <div>4 VPCS</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="device-item">
                        <div class="device-icon">🔀</div>
                        <div>1 Layer 2 Switch</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="device-item">
                        <div class="device-icon">🔄</div>
                        <div>1 Router</div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="connection-guide">
                <p><strong>Make these connections:</strong></p>
                <div class="connection-visual">
                    <div class="connection-line">
                        <span>PC1 & PC2</span> <span class="arrow">→</span> <span>Switch (Ports 1 & 2)</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="connection-line">
                        <span>PC3 & PC4</span> <span class="arrow">→</span> <span>Switch (Ports 3 & 4)</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="connection-line">
                        <span>Switch (Port 5)</span> <span class="arrow">→</span> <span>Router</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="note-box">
                <div class="note-icon">💡</div>
                <div class="note-text">
                    <strong>VLAN Concept:</strong> We'll create two VLANs (10 and 20) to separate our PCs into different broadcast domains.
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="setup-step">
        <div class="step-header">
            <span class="step-number">2</span>
            <h3>Configure VLANs on the Switch</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="step-content">
            <div class="instruction-card important">
                <div class="instruction-icon">⌨️</div>
                <div class="instruction-text">
                    Access the switch CLI by right-clicking and selecting <span class="highlight">Console</span>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="config-section">
                <div class="device-config">
                    <h4>Create VLANs</h4>
                    <div class="code-block">
                        <div class="code-header">Enter these commands:</div>
                        <code>enable</code>
                        <code>configure terminal</code>
                        <code>vlan 10</code>
                        <code>name SALES</code>
                        <code>vlan 20</code>
                        <code>name MARKETING</code>
                        <code>exit</code>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="device-config">
                    <h4>Assign Ports to VLANs</h4>
                    <div class="code-block">
                        <div class="code-header">Configure access ports:</div>
                        <code>interface range fastEthernet 0/1-2</code>
                        <code>switchport mode access</code>
                        <code>switchport access vlan 10</code>
                        <code>interface range fastEthernet 0/3-4</code>
                        <code>switchport mode access</code>
                        <code>switchport access vlan 20</code>
                        <code>exit</code>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="config-section">
                <div class="device-config full-width">
                    <h4>Configure Trunk Port (to Router)</h4>
                    <div class="code-block">
                        <div class="code-header">Set up trunking:</div>
                        <code>interface fastEthernet 0/5</code>
                        <code>switchport mode trunk</code>
                        <code>switchport trunk allowed vlan 10,20</code>
                        <code>end</code>
                        <code>write memory</code>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="verification">
                <p>Verify your VLAN configuration:</p>
                <div class="code-block">
                    <code>show vlan brief</code>
                </div>
                <div class="expected-output">
                    <p><strong>Expected Output:</strong></p>
                    <pre>VLAN Name       Status    Ports
---- ---------- -------- --------------------------
1    default    active   Fa0/5
10   SALES      active   Fa0/1, Fa0/2
20   MARKETING  active   Fa0/3, Fa0/4</pre>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="setup-step">
        <div class="step-header">
            <span class="step-number">3</span>
            <h3>Configure Router-on-a-Stick</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="step-content">
            <div class="instruction-card important">
                <div class="instruction-icon">🔄</div>
                <div class="instruction-text">
                    Access the router CLI to configure inter-VLAN routing
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="config-section">
                <div class="device-config full-width">
                    <h4>Create Subinterfaces</h4>
                    <div class="code-block">
                        <div class="code-header">Configure router interfaces:</div>
                        <code>enable</code>
                        <code>configure terminal</code>
                        <code>interface gigabitEthernet 0/0</code>
                        <code>no shutdown</code>
                        <code>exit</code>
                        <code>interface gigabitEthernet 0/0.10</code>
                        <code>encapsulation dot1Q 10</code>
                        <code>ip address 192.168.10.1 255.255.255.0</code>
                        <code>interface gigabitEthernet 0/0.20</code>
                        <code>encapsulation dot1Q 20</code>
                        <code>ip address 192.168.20.1 255.255.255.0</code>
                        <code>end</code>
                        <code>write memory</code>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="note-box tip">
                <div class="note-icon">🔍</div>
                <div class="note-text">
                    <strong>Router-on-a-Stick:</strong> This configuration allows a single physical router interface to route traffic between multiple VLANs using subinterfaces.
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="setup-step">
        <div class="step-header">
            <span class="step-number">4</span>
            <h3>Configure PCs and Test Connectivity</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="step-content">
            <div class="config-section">
                <div class="device-config">
                    <h4>VLAN 10 PCs (Sales)</h4>
                    <div class="code-block">
                        <div class="code-header">PC1 Configuration:</div>
                        <code>ip 192.168.10.2 255.255.255.0 192.168.10.1</code>
                    </div>
                    <div class="code-block">
                        <div class="code-header">PC2 Configuration:</div>
                        <code>ip 192.168.10.3 255.255.255.0 192.168.10.1</code>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="device-config">
                    <h4>VLAN 20 PCs (Marketing)</h4>
                    <div class="code-block">
                        <div class="code-header">PC3 Configuration:</div>
                        <code>ip 192.168.20.2 255.255.255.0 192.168.20.1</code>
                    </div>
                    <div class="code-block">
                        <div class="code-header">PC4 Configuration:</div>
                        <code>ip 192.168.20.3 255.255.255.0 192.168.20.1</code>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="test-instructions">
                <h4>Testing Your VLAN Configuration</h4>

                <div class="test-case">
                    <div class="test-number">1</div>
                    <div class="test-content">
                        <p><strong>Test intra-VLAN communication:</strong></p>
                        <div class="code-block">
                            <code>ping 192.168.10.3</code> <span class="comment"># From PC1 to PC2 (should work)</span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="test-case">
                    <div class="test-number">2</div>
                    <div class="test-content">
                        <p><strong>Test inter-VLAN communication:</strong></p>
                        <div class="code-block">
                            <code>ping 192.168.20.2</code> <span class="comment"># From PC1 to PC3 (should work through router)</span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="test-case">
                    <div class="test-number">3</div>
                    <div class="test-content">
                        <p><strong>Verify isolation:</strong></p>
                        <div class="code-block">
                            <code>show mac-address-table</code> <span class="comment"># On switch to see VLAN separation</span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="completion-message success">
        <h3>🎉 VLAN Mastery Achieved!</h3>
        <p>You've successfully configured VLANs, trunking, and inter-VLAN routing!</p>
        <div class="next-steps">
            <p><strong>Challenge:</strong> Try adding a third VLAN for the IT department!</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>



